    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling output today, led by **Junior Caminero** (69.28), who holds our top slot against Jos\u00e9 Soriano. **Caminero** benefits from a favorable park factor and a solid lineup position, making him our primary engine for RBI and R production. We are also leaning heavily into our speed-focused outfielders, with **Christian Yelich** (62.88) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (61.45) anchoring the group. Despite the risk of elite opposing catchers, both players gain significant leverage from their leadoff spots and dynamic platoon advantages against Trevor McDonald and Aaron Nola, respectively. **Yordan Alvarez** (63.50) remains a must-start despite a neutral platoon matchup, as his elite xwOBA of 0.452 keeps his floor significantly higher than the rest of the utility-tier pool.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Caleb Durbin** (45.34), who barely missed the cut. While **Durbin** provides the elite speed profile we covet, the optimizer flagged the extreme difficulty of his matchup against Jacob deGrom. The combination of a high-tier opponent SP_xERA and a negative \"Elite Hold\" warning for SB risk tipped the scales toward **Luke Raley** (52.86), whose favorable park factors and platoon edge against Cade Cavalli offered a safer projection for efficiency. We are closely monitoring the \"Lineup Pending\" status for **Dillon Dingler** and **Casey Schmitt**; while both are projected to start, any downward shift in their batting order could necessitate a quick pivot to ensure we maintain our daily efficiency targets. Owners should note that **Colt Keith** (50.45) faces a negative platoon adjustment today, but he retains his spot as a fringe starter due to the favorable 4.35 xERA of Joey Cantillo.",
